From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] explorer: the taskbar started at a raised scale scales its text and icons once

The taskbar sizes everything by the display scale through SG_PX (0832),
and takes its text from the menu font and its icons' size from
SM_CXSMICON. Explorer is aware of the DPI, so Wine gives it those already
at the scale it started with; SG_PX scaled them a second time. Started at
100% (every machine until now) the two agree. Signed in at 175% -- a
Surface Pro 7's 2736x1824 screen at its recommended scale (sg-session
sg_auto_scale; David 2026-10-05: "everything is tiny") -- the clock's text
was 1.75 x 1.75 times its size and the date ran off the bar's end, the
buttons' titles and icons too large. Both are taken back to 100% first
(sg_unscaled), then scaled once. A button's icon larger than the small
icon the process was given (the scale raised after it started) is the
large icon made smaller, not the small one blown up.

Test: test/barhidpi-gate.sh with test/barscale-probe.c (mutant
SG_MUTANT_BAR_TWICE); test/barscale-gate.sh still passes.
---
--- a/programs/explorer/systray.c
+++ b/programs/explorer/systray.c
@@ -154,13 +154,25 @@
 #else
 #define SG_PX(v) (v)
 #endif
-#define SG_SMICON SG_PX(GetSystemMetrics( SM_CXSMICON ))
+/* Stained Glass OS: a size Wine gives this process (the system metrics, the
+ * menu font) at the display scale it started with, back at 100%: SG_PX
+ * scales it again. Started at 175% (sign-in on a 2736x1824 screen), the
+ * text and icons were scaled twice -- the date ran off the bar's end. */
+static int sg_unscaled( int v )
+{
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_BAR_TWICE
+    UINT dpi = GetDpiForSystem();
+    if (dpi > 96) return MulDiv( v, 96, dpi );
+#endif
+    return v;
+}
+#define SG_SMICON SG_PX(sg_unscaled( GetSystemMetrics( SM_CXSMICON ) ))
 
 /* the bar's text: the menu font, as large as the bar is */
 static HFONT sg_bar_font( const LOGFONTW *base )
 {
     LOGFONTW lf = *base;
-    lf.lfHeight = SG_PX(lf.lfHeight);
+    lf.lfHeight = SG_PX(sg_unscaled( lf.lfHeight ));
     return CreateFontIndirectW( &lf );
 }
 
@@ -3160,8 +3172,11 @@
     sg_look_frame( hdc, &rect, state );
     {
         BOOL big = sg_look == SG_LOOK_GLASS && win->icon_only && !sg_bar.small && !sg_vertical();
-        HICON icon = big && win->exe_icon_big ? win->exe_icon_big : win->exe_icon;
         int cx = big ? SG_PX(32) : SG_SMICON, cy = cx;
+        /* larger than the small icon this process was given (the scale was
+         * raised after it started): the large one, made smaller, not the
+         * small one blown up */
+        HICON icon = (big || cx > GetSystemMetrics( SM_CXSMICON )) && win->exe_icon_big ? win->exe_icon_big : win->exe_icon;
         if (!icon) icon = LoadIconW( 0, (const WCHAR *)IDI_APPLICATION );
         if (icon && win->icon_only)
             DrawIconEx( hdc, rect.left + (rect.right - rect.left - cx) / 2, rect.top + (rect.bottom - rect.top - cy) / 2,
